# ADR 0012 wording: "mask" (meaning a program's UI documentation) -> "frontend".
# NOT touched: ticket/table/form masks, CSS clip-path masks, the otp-input `mask` attribute.
# Usage: python3 scripts/replace.py --scope docs/en --rules scripts/rules/masks_to_frontends_text.rules [--apply]

# path texts in prose and code spans
\bmasks/ => frontends/
\bskins/ => frontends/
# old file names in link labels / file lists
\[structure\.md\] => [layout.md]
\[menu\.md\] => [menus.md]
`structure\.md` => `layout.md`
`menu\.md` => `menus.md`
# headings and fixed phrases
\bMask [Dd]ocumentation\b => Frontend documentation
\bmask documentation\b => frontend documentation
\bMask directory\b => Frontend directory
\b(Wiki|Desktop|CRM|CRM/ERP) masks\b => \1 frontends
\bPrograms \(masks\) => Programs (frontends)
\bcomponents, masks and\b => components, frontends and
\bprograms, components and masks\b => programs, components and frontends
\bimports and masks\b => imports and frontends
`api.md` per mask\b => `api.md` per frontend
\bmask APIs\b => frontend APIs
\bas a mask\b => as a frontend
\*\*Predictability\*\*: masks => **Predictability**: frontends
\bdesktop masks — API => desktop frontends — API
# "skin" is the pre-ADR-0007 word for the same thing (skin tone etc. excluded)
\bSkins\b(?![ -]?(tone|and gender)) => Frontends
\bSkin\b(?![ -]?(tone|and gender)) => Frontend
\bskins\b(?![ -]?(tone|and gender)) => frontends
\bskin\b(?![ -]?(tone|and gender)) => frontend
